# The address YOUR PC uses to reach this machine.
#
# Get it from an SSH session on this box:
#     echo $SSH_CONNECTION
# The third of the four values is the answer. By definition it is an address
# that works from your PC, because it is the one you are connected on.
#
# Where the WireGuard tunnel terminates decides what this looks like:
#   - tunnel ends on this box       -> a tunnel address, e.g. 10.0.0.1
#   - tunnel ends on the router and
#     this box sits on the LAN      -> the LAN address, e.g. 192.168.2.69
# Both are correct. Use whichever one you actually SSH to.
#
# Clients are told to open the game socket at this address, so 127.0.0.1 is
# always wrong here - it would send every client to itself, which looks like
# a server list that loads followed by a connection that never completes.
SERVER_ADDRESS=10.0.0.1
